    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing OCR Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Vision AI as the OCR provider for this project. The goal is to incorporate it directly into `extract_text.py`.\n\n\n**Defining OCR Logic**\n\nI've outlined the logic for the `extract_text.py` script. The plan is to read an image, use `ImageAnnotatorClient` with `text_detection`, and extract the text from the response. I'm focusing on incorporating `google.cloud.vision_v1p3beta1` for OCR and assuming the user has handled authentication, such as using environment variables. Next, I'll start building the Python code with placeholders for the image path and comprehensive error handling.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865021233,
          "start": 1789865018127
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc44c30f001Q23lzC3TtwnUea",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc44bec2001u2x7chPspYzmkZ",
      "session_id": "ses_f43bb41baffeZA205TqqN2CPIu",
      "time_created": 1789865018127,
      "time_updated": 1789865021234
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "5dcAzAc3rD8Y1FPA",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import os\nimport io\nfrom google.cloud import vision\n\ndef extract_text_from_image(image_path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts plain text from a scanned document image using Google Cloud Vision API.\n\n    Args:\n        image_path (str): The path to the image file.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The extracted text, or an empty string if no text is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Instantiates a client\n    client = vision.ImageAnnotatorClient()\n\n    # Loads the image into memory\n    with io.open(image_path, 'rb') as image_file:\n        content = image_file.read()\n\n    image = vision.Image(content=content)\n\n    # Performs text detection on the image\n    response = client.document_text_detection(image=image)\n    \n    # Extract the full text annotation\n    if response.full_text_annotation:\n        return response.full_text_annotation.text\n    else:\n        return \"\"\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Replace 'path/to/your/image.jpg' with the actual path to your scanned document image\n    # Ensure GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable is set or\n    # authenticate appropriately for Google Cloud Vision API.\n    # For example: export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=\"/path/to/your/keyfile.json\"\n    image_file_path = 'path/to/your/image.jpg' \n\n    if not os.path.exists(image_file_path):\n        print(f\"Error: Image file not found at {image_file_path}\")\n    else:\n        extracted_text = extract_text_from_image(image_file_path)\n        if extracted_text:\n            print(\"Extracted Text:\")\n            print(extracted_text)\n        else:\n            print(\"No text was extracted from the image.\")\n",
            "filePath": "extract_text.py"
          },
